Subject: profile FLOPs on a CPU copy - stats() crashes on single-GPU runs

det_solver.fit() calls stats(cfg) AFTER BaseSolver.train() has moved the model
to CUDA. stats() deep-copies that CUDA model, but calflops builds its dummy
input on CPU, so the informational FLOPs forward dies with "Expected all
tensors to be on the same device" before training starts (hit live on the
5090 pod, 2026-09-02, first RTv4 person_v2 launch). Move the throwaway copy
to CPU: the profile is device-agnostic and the real model is untouched.
---
--- a/engine/misc/profiler_utils.py
+++ b/engine/misc/profiler_utils.py
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ def stats(
     base_size = cfg.train_dataloader.collate_fn.base_size
     input_shape = (1, 3, base_size, base_size)

-    model_for_info = copy.deepcopy(cfg.model).deploy()
+    model_for_info = copy.deepcopy(cfg.model).deploy().to("cpu")

     flops, macs, _ = calculate_flops(model=model_for_info,
                                         input_shape=input_shape,
